Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:21:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] B70-Q27-0006: DFlash2 shortlist draft vocab
 (B70_DFLASH_DRAFT_VOCAB)

B70_DFLASH_DRAFT_VOCAB=<token id file> gives the DFlash2 drafter of a Qwen3_5 target
its own small head: the target lm_head rows of a token shortlist, used only for the
drafter's candidate top-k. The target keeps its full-vocab head (B70_HEAD_FP8
included) and verifies against the full distribution, so the output distribution is
unchanged: DFlash2's q is already supported on the K candidates only and the walk and
the rejection read the same cached scores; the shortlist only changes which K ids.

Rows are balanced over TP ranks (position i -> rank i % tp), exchanged once at load
over the TP gloo group from the BF16 shards; under B70_HEAD_FP8=1 on XPU the copy is
FP8 W8A16 with the target's per-row recipe. One-time log "B70 DFlash draft vocab: <n>
tokens". Unset -> nothing built, stock compute_candidates. LiLiCorr and non-Qwen3_5
targets (Flash-Next Qwen4Exp) are off. Idea: steveseguin/b70-optimization-lab R294.

CPU tests: closed-form single-position exactness (20 cases), two-position block
chi-square (shortlist p=0.39, full-vocab p=0.35, inconsistent-q negative control
chi2=23680), head == full-vocab top-k on the shortlist at TP1/TP2 (gloo), off paths.
